-- title:
--   Lemma 4.1 — estimation on the change of $\Lambda^k(u,p)$ (corrected: $k\ge2$, $u^{k-1}\in U$)
-- statement:
--   Let $E,F$ be finite-dimensional real inner product spaces, $U\subseteq E$ a closed convex set, $C\subseteq F$ a closed convex cone with dual cone $C^*=\{p:\langle x,p\rangle\ge0\ \forall x\in C\}$, and let $G:E\to E$, $J:E\to(-\infty,+\infty]$, $\Theta:E\to F$ satisfy the standing assumptions: $G$ is $L$-Lipschitz on $U$, $J$ is proper convex l.s.c., $\Theta$ is $C$-convex and $\tau$-Lipschitz on $U$ ($\tau>0$). Let the parameters satisfy $\frac{\sqrt5-1}{2}\le\eta<1$, $0<\gamma<1/\tau$, $0<\alpha\le\frac{1}{2(\gamma\tau^2+L+\tau)\eta}$, and let $\{(v^k,u^k,p^k,q^k)\}$ be generated by ALAVI (25)–(28) from arbitrary $u^1,v^0,p^1$.
--
--   Let $\Lambda^k$ be the Lyapunov function (31), $L_{u^*}$ the Lagrangian (4), and $\rho=\min\{\frac{\eta}{2\alpha(1-\eta)^2},\frac\tau2,\frac{1-\tau\gamma}{2\gamma},\frac1\gamma\}$. Then $\rho>0$, and for every $k\ge2$ with $u^{k-1}\in U$, all $(u,p)\in(U\cap\operatorname{dom}J)\times C^*$ and every $u^*\in E$,
--
--   $$
--   \Lambda^k(u,p)-\Lambda^{k+1}(u,p)\ge\big[L_{u^*}(u^k,p)-L_{u^*}(u,q^k)\big]+\langle G(u^k)-G(u^*),u^k-u\rangle+\rho\big[\|w^{k-1}-w^k\|^2+\|p^k-q^k\|^2\big],
--   $$
--
--   where $w=(v,u,p)$ and $\|w^{k-1}-w^k\|^2=\|v^{k-1}-v^k\|^2+\|u^{k-1}-u^k\|^2+\|p^{k-1}-p^k\|^2$.
--
--   This is the Lyapunov estimate on which the convergence analysis of ALAVI (Theorem 1) rests.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - generalization: ℝⁿ and ℝᵐ with the Euclidean inner product → finite-dimensional real inner product spaces E, F; reason: ℝⁿ, ℝᵐ are instances and no coordinate is used, so the statement specializes to the page's
--   - generalization: G continuous on ℝⁿ and L-Lipschitz on U (H2); Θ continuous on ℝⁿ and τ-Lipschitz on an open O ⊇ U (H5) → G L-Lipschitz on U and Θ τ-Lipschitz on U, nothing assumed off U; reason: the proofs evaluate G and Θ only at points of U; the page's hypotheses imply these
--   - reading: J "a continuous function on U" (p.2) and "proper convex l.s.c." (H3, p.4) → J : E → (−∞, +∞] proper, convex, lower semicontinuous (IsProperConvexLSC); reason: the two printed descriptions differ; (H3) is the one the proofs use, and a convex J continuous on the closed set U, extended by +∞, satisfies it
--   - encoding: real values J(u) → (J u).toReal at points of dom J (effDom J); reason: J is finite wherever the statement evaluates it; at points outside dom J the printed inequalities read +∞ ≥ 0
--   - encoding: C a nonempty closed convex cone; C∗ (never defined on the page); Π the projection onto C∗ → C : ProperCone ℝ F; C∗ = ProperCone.innerDual C; Π = CalamaiMore.Convergence.proj onto C∗; reason: every nonempty closed convex cone is a ProperCone; C∗ is used as the dual cone {p | ⟨x, p⟩ ≥ 0 ∀ x ∈ C} (p.7, Example A.4); the projection onto the nonempty closed convex C∗ exists
--   - generalization: ALAVI input u¹, v⁰ ∈ ℝⁿ, p⁰ ∈ ℝᵐ, with p¹ read in (26) at k = 1 but never defined → u¹, v⁰ and p¹ arbitrary; reason: covers both readings p¹ = Π(p⁰ + γΘ(u¹)) and p¹ = p⁰
--   - generalization: u∗ a solution of (VIP) → u∗ any point of E; reason: G(u∗) cancels from the inequality, so the choice of u∗ plays no role
--   - correction: k = 1, 2, … with u¹ ∈ ℝⁿ arbitrary → 2 ≤ k and uᵏ⁻¹ ∈ U; reason: at k = 1 the statement is undefined; at k = 2 the Lipschitz steps (42)–(43) need u¹ ∈ U, which the input does not give, and Lemma 4.1 is false without it: U = [0,1] ⊂ ℝ, C = ℝ₊, J = 0, Θ(u) = u, G(u) = −100·max(0, −1/2 − u) (zero on U, so L = 0), η = 0.7, γ = 1/2, α = 0.1, u¹ = −2, v⁰ = 0, p¹ = 2, (u, p) = (0, 0) ∈ S_MVIS give Λ²(0,0) − Λ³(0,0) = 3.87 < 4.87 = right-hand side; for k ≥ 3, uᵏ⁻¹ ∈ U holds automatically
--   - encoding: ‖wᵏ⁻¹ − wᵏ‖² for the stacked vector w = (v, u, p) → ‖vᵏ⁻¹ − vᵏ‖² + ‖uᵏ⁻¹ − uᵏ‖² + ‖pᵏ⁻¹ − pᵏ‖²; reason: the Euclidean norm of the stacked vector, written out (Mathlib's norm on a product is the sup norm)
-- source:
--   Zhao, Zhu & Zhang, An Augmented Lagrangian Approach to Conically Constrained Non-monotone Variational Inequality Problems, arXiv:2306.01214v1, Lemma 4.1, p.13 (proof pp.13–17)

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_GoldenRatioVI_Fixed_solutionSet
import Definitions.Def_CalamaiMore_Convergence_proj
import Definitions.Def_ALAVI_Standing
import Definitions.Def_ALAVI_Params
import Definitions.Def_ALAVI_IsALAVIRun
import Definitions.Def_ALAVI_Lag
import Definitions.Def_ALAVI_lam
import Definitions.Def_ALAVI_rho

namespace ALAVI

/-- **Lemma 4.1 (Estimation on the change of Λᵏ(u, p)).** Under Assumption A and
`(√5 - 1)/2 ≤ η < 1`, `0 < γ < 1/τ`, `0 < α ≤ 1/(2(γτ² + L + τ)η)`, for a run of ALAVI, every
`k ≥ 2` with `uᵏ⁻¹ ∈ U` and all `(w, b) ∈ (U ∩ dom J) × C*`:
`ρ > 0` and
`Λᵏ(w, b) - Λᵏ⁺¹(w, b) ≥ [L_{u*}(uᵏ, b) - L_{u*}(w, qᵏ)] + ⟨G(uᵏ) - G(u*), uᵏ - w⟩`
`  + ρ[‖wᵏ⁻¹ - wᵏ‖² + ‖pᵏ - qᵏ‖²]`,
where `‖wᵏ⁻¹ - wᵏ‖² = ‖vᵏ⁻¹ - vᵏ‖² + ‖uᵏ⁻¹ - uᵏ‖² + ‖pᵏ⁻¹ - pᵏ‖²` (Euclidean norm of the
stacked vector `w = (v, u, p)`) and `ρ = min{η/(2α(1-η)²), τ/2, (1-τγ)/(2γ), 1/γ}`.

Zhao, Zhu & Zhang, arXiv:2306.01214v1, Lemma 4.1, p.13 (proof pp.13–17).

Formalization Notes: the page states it for `k = 1, 2, …`; at `k = 1` it reads `u⁰`, `p⁰` and (32)
at iteration `0`, which do not exist, so `k ≥ 2`. At `k = 2` the Lipschitz step (42)–(43) needs
`u¹ ∈ U`, which the input does not give; hence `uᵏ⁻¹ ∈ U` (automatic for `k ≥ 3`). `u*` is any
point (the page takes a solution of (VIP); `G(u*)` cancels). `w` is restricted to `dom J`, where
`J(w)` is finite. `‖wᵏ⁻¹ - wᵏ‖²` is written out as a sum of three squares, not Mathlib's sup norm
on a product. -/
theorem lemma_4_1 {E F : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E] [FiniteDimensional ℝ E]
    [NormedAddCommGroup F] [InnerProductSpace ℝ F] [FiniteDimensional ℝ F]
    (U : Set E) (C : ProperCone ℝ F) (G : E → E) (J : E → EReal) (Θ : E → F) (L τ η α γ : ℝ) (v u : ℕ → E) (p q : ℕ → F)
    (hA : Standing U C G J Θ L τ) (hP : Params η α γ L τ)
    (hrun : IsALAVIRun U C G J Θ η α γ v u p q)
    (k : ℕ) (hk : 2 ≤ k) (hk1 : u (k - 1) ∈ U) (a : E) (ha : a ∈ U) (haJ : a ∈ GoldenRatioVI.Fixed.effDom J)
    (b : F) (hb : b ∈ ProperCone.innerDual (C : Set F)) (ustar : E) :
    0 < rho η α γ τ ∧
      (Lag G J Θ ustar (u k) b - Lag G J Θ ustar a (q k)) + inner ℝ (G (u k) - G ustar) (u k - a) +
          rho η α γ τ * (‖v (k - 1) - v k‖ ^ 2 + ‖u (k - 1) - u k‖ ^ 2 + ‖p (k - 1) - p k‖ ^ 2 +
          ‖p k - q k‖ ^ 2) ≤
        lam η α γ L τ v u p k a b - lam η α γ L τ v u p (k + 1) a b := by sorry

end ALAVI
